326		The game $\mathfrak{G}^{\mathrm{Pauli}}$ (also $\mathfrak{G}^{\mathrm{Pauli}}_{\mathsf{qldparams}}$) is parametrized by an admissible tuple $\mathsf{qldparams} = (q,m,d)$ (Definition~\ref{def:admissible}): admissibility makes $q$ a power of $2$, so that the field $\F_q$, its fixed identification with binary strings (Chapter~\ref{chap:qpbt-algebra}), and the trace $\tr\colon \F_q \to \F_2$ used by the win predicate below are defined, and it provides the divisibility $m \mid q$ required by the index map $\chi$ of Definition~\ref{def:ld-question-distribution}. The question type set is
